From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-eip: use upstream Qualcomm SoC headers

The downstream soc/qcom/socinfo.h compatibility header is not part of
upstream Linux.  Kernels newer than 6.1 use qcom_smem_get_soc_id(), whose
declaration is provided by linux/soc/qcom/smem.h, so the downstream include
is both unused and invalid.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/tree/10a89a95f814cd325e23105f102428644f45014f
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
--- a/driver/exports/eip.h
+++ b/driver/exports/eip.h
@@ -21,7 +21,6 @@
 #include <crypto/aead.h>
 #include <crypto/skcipher.h>
 #include <crypto/hash.h>
-#include <soc/qcom/socinfo.h>
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE > KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 0))
 #include <dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/smem.h>
--- a/clients/crypto/eip_crypto.c
+++ b/clients/crypto/eip_crypto.c
@@ -19,7 +19,6 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/crypto.h>
-#include <soc/qcom/socinfo.h>
 
 #include "eip_crypto.h"
 
